| `fused_mm: installed forward override` | 128 | 해당 없음 |\\n| `offload_compressed` fallback | `fused_mm: offload fused unsupported for per-threshold codec P4FlatCompressor` | 128 | 160 |\\n\\nCount는 해당 weight state를 쓰는 cell에서의 값이며 KV state가 바뀌어도\\n같다. Raw-weight cell은 override와 fallback 모두 0이다.\\n\\n현재 batch-1 P4Flat matrix의 route 기대값은 다음과 같다.\\n\\n| 기능 | OFF | ON |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Weight offload | `WLoad=0` | `WLoad>0` |\\n| KV offload | `KVLoad=0` | `KVLoad>0` |\\n| Weight compression | `WDecomp=0` | fused override이면 `WDecomp=0`, dense fallback이면 `WDecomp>0` |\\n| KV compression | `KVDecomp=0` | `KVDecomp>0` |\\n\\n`O>0`은 offload capacity만 뜻한다. KV 검증에는 요청이 실제 offloadable\\nblock을 사용하고 `KVLoad>0`이어야 한다.\\n\\n## 6. 검증 범위\\n\\n이 matrix는 correctness와 route smoke다.\\n\\n- `--time-breakdown`이 켜진 계측 실행이므로 성능 비교 자료가 아니다.\\n- Exact-token 검사는 한 matrix 실행 안의 cell 간 비교다. Race 검증에는\\n  matrix 자체를 여러 번 실행해 artifact를 비교해야 한다.\\n- 70B에서는 weight-offload OFF 여섯 valid cell을 검증하지 않는다.\\n- Fused-MM은 고정 ON이며 별도 ON/OFF 축은 아니다. 현재 P4Flat\\n  `offload_compressed` cell은 명시적인 dense fallback을 사용하므로 70B\\n  matrix는 fused request와 fallback을 검증한다.\\n- ATS와 `--reduce-kv-footprint`는 별도 실험이므로 matrix에서 제외한다.\\n- Mixed-prefill은 기본적으로 raw secondary KV를 읽을 수 있다.\\n  `vllm_offload_kvweight_prefill.py`는 해당 phase와 active-block 진단용이며\\n  기본 answer matrix를 대신하지 않는다.\\n\\n성능은 correctness 통과 후 동일한 topology로 별도 normal pass를 최소\\n3회 실행한다. 예를 들어 생성 길이를 `--gen 129 --warmup 16`으로 늘리고\\nnormal pass에는 `--time-breakdown`을 사용하지 않는다. 원인 분석이 필요할\\n때만 같은 조건의 별도 instrumentation pass를 추가한다.\\n\\n## CD3 KV의 무손실 4bit exponent delta 실험\\n\\nCD3 weight는 기존 3bit를 유지하고, `chunk_delta3` KV의 exponent delta만\\n3bit(기본값) 또는 4bit로 선택할 수 있다. Sign/mantissa와 범위 밖 exponent는\\n그대로 보존하므로 두 경우 모두 BF16 비트 단위 무손실이다.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Offline: 기존 실험 인자에 다음 옵션을 추가한다.\\nbash scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --methods cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp --cd3-kv-delta-bits 4\\n\\n# Serving: CD3 kvcomp cell에만 적용된다.\\nbash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp --cd3-kv-delta-bits 4\\n```\\n\\n동일한 인자에 `--cd3-kv-delta-bits 3`을 주어 기준 실험과 비교한다.\\nSuite는 상속된 환경변수를 지우므로 이 CLI 옵션을 사용해야 한다.\\nDriver를 직접 실행할 때는 Python 시작 전에\\n`TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_DELTA_BITS=4`를 설정한다. 실행 중 변경은 지원하지 않는다.\\n첫 실행은 해당 KV 비트 폭의 C++/CUDA extension을 빌드한다.\\n\\n4bit는 16개 코드를 8바이트로 패킹하여 NEON 패킹과 GPU 정렬 로드를\\n단순화한다. 대신 고정 body가 값당 1bit 커지고 exponent 범위는 8개에서\\n16개로 넓어진다. 같은 base-sharing 설정에서 예외율 감소가 약 4.69%p를\\n넘으면 예외 저장량 감소가 추가 code bytes를 상쇄한다\\n(Packed20 예외 3개당 8바이트, 끝부분 반올림 제외).\\nH2D byte 수, CPU encode, GPU decode와 전체 latency를 함께 비교한다.\\n기존 split-H2D 기준과 decode thread 수의 최적값은 달라질 수 있다.\\n\\n### CD3 KV 공통 decode 최적화와 thread 선택\\n\\n3bit/4bit KV는 BF16 두 값을 한 32bit 정수로 함께 복원한다. 예외가 없는\\n타일은 CTA 전체가 같은 조건으로 동기화 없이 종료하고, 예외가 있는 타일은\\nbase store 이후 동기화와 Packed20 patch를 유지한다. Weight decoder와\\nfused-MM은 기존 경로를 유지한다.\\n\\nKV decoder thread 수는 weight의 `TIERED_SERVE_CD3_DECODE_THREADS`와 분리했다.\\nDriver 직접 실행 시 `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_DECODE_THREADS=64|128`을 Python 시작\\n전에 지정한다. Suite에서는 `--cd3-kv-decode-threads auto|64|128`을 사용한다.\\n`auto`는 native 기본값을 사용하며 현재는 128이다. 실제 선택값은 KV buffer\\n초기화 로그의 `decode_threads`에 표시된다.\\n\\nGH200의 실제 KV 1536블록 비교에서 128이 64보다 빨라 기본값 128을 유지한다.\\n256은 기존 측정 결과에 대한 사용자 지시에 따라 이번 탐색에서 제외했다.\\n작은 batch의 CPU launch 공백이 포함된 event 시간만으로 기본값을 바꾸지 않는다.\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --methods cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp --cd3-kv-delta-bits 3 \\\\\\n  --cd3-kv-decode-threads 128\\n\\nbash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp --cd3-kv-delta-bits 4 \\\\\\n  --cd3-kv-decode-threads 128\\n```\\n# KV load metrics\\n\\n`scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh` enables KV byte counters, GPU timing,\\nand CSV output only with `--breakdown`. Normal serving runs disable collection\\nand record `-` in the suite's `kv_metrics_csv` field.\\n\\n`scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh` collects KV byte counters by default\\nand enables GPU timing with `--breakdown`. When collection is enabled, each run\\nhas a `kv_metrics` directory containing per-worker forward CSVs and `summary.csv`;\\nthe suite's `summary.tsv` links the latter as `kv_metrics_csv`. Offline also\\nincludes the byte totals and ratios in its GPU breakdown CSV with `--breakdown`.\\n\\n| Field | Meaning |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `kv_raw_bytes` | Dense BF16 K+V bytes corresponding to the requested KV being loaded. |\\n| `kv_payload_bytes` | Active encoded KV payload bytes, including raw fallback payloads. |\\n| `kv_h2d_bytes` | Sum of bytes actually submitted to H2D copies, including routing metadata, alignment and any additional rows/entries copied. This is not physical link-protocol traffic. |\\n| `kv_compression_ratio` | `sum(kv_raw_bytes) / sum(kv_payload_bytes)`. |\\n| `kv_transfer_ratio` | `sum(kv_raw_bytes) / sum(kv_h2d_bytes)`. |\\n| `kvload_ms` | Sum of the GPU elapsed time of individual H2D submission windows for that forward. |\\n\\nThe active payload is CD3 body rows, active Packed20 entry words and CSR\\noffsets; P4Flat's selected `total_size` values; or ZipServ's selected bitmap,\\noffset and variable payload sizes. Raw payloads have compression ratio 1.\\nRepeated loads count repeatedly: these are traffic-weighted ratios of the KV\\nbeing loaded, not an inventory of all KV stored in memory. Raw span coalescing\\ncan copy holes, so its transfer ratio need not be 1. Empty transfers have zero\\nbytes and an undefined (`NA`) ratio.\\n\\nTiming is enabled only by the suites' existing `--breakdown` option. Its begin\\nand end events bracket memcpy submission after host preparation and existing\\nbuffer dependencies. Decompression and preceding ring waits are excluded.\\nResource contention and exposed submission gaps inside the window remain\\nincluded. Windows on different streams can overlap; their sum is not an\\nadditive decomposition of GPU forward time or pure copy-engine activity.\\n`KVLoadResidualEstimate` preserves the old union-minus-weight calculation as a\\ndiagnostic only. `ExposedLoad` uses the new windows too and remains a window\\noverlap metric, not GPU idle time.\\n\\nCounters use CPU metadata and native copy descriptors. They do not copy sizes\\nback from the GPU or add synchronization. Event pairs and counter slots are\\nreused, including distinct slots for multiple chunks of one layer. CSV output\\noccurs once per completed host forward, not per layer. Timing readback never\\nwaits; unfinished timing is `NA`. Existing diagnostic breakdown synchronization\\nis unchanged. The offline CPU diagnostic CSV still exposes CD3 plan/native\\npreparation and staging costs separately.\\n\\nRaw, CD3, P4Flat (including its shared UBLB staging), and ZipServ paths are\\naccounted, including mixed prefill and raw fallbacks. Optional codecs without\\nbyte accounting produce `bytes_complete=0` and `NA`, never a fabricated zero.\\nSummary rows require complete coverage; `bytes_complete_forwards` and\\n`timed_forwards` expose missing data.\\n\\nSummaries group by config, offline batch and phase. Offline forward CSVs also\\ncarry the driver's step index. Summary byte sums include the recorded warmup\\nsteps; the existing offline GPU breakdown retains its own decode warmup\\nexclusion. Serving counters cover all recorded model forwards, including\\nstartup requests and the drain, and are not trimmed to the client's request\\ncohort. They must not be divided by trimmed client token totals.\\n\\nFor direct runner use, set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_METRICS=1` and\\n`TIERED_SERVE_KV_METRICS_DIR=/path/to/output`. `TIERED_SERVE_COLLECT_TIME=1`\\nalso enables event timing. Updated native bindings are built by the existing\\nextension loader on the next launch; allow for the first-launch rebuild.\\n# CD3 KV hybrid storage\\n\\nCD3 KV defaults to **CSR compact / serial** after the\\n[2026-09-24 selection](../cd3_algorithm_selection.md). Weight compression\\nand the selected 3-bit/4-bit KV codec are unchanged. Hybrid remains an explicit\\ncomparison path; its real serving confirmation failed in native batch-copy\\nsubmission and it is not qualified for the current operating selection.\\nThese options affect the CD3 KV-compressed method only.\\n\\n| Comparison | Storage | CSR policy | Execution |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| A baseline | `csr` | `append` | `serial` |\\n| B default | `csr` | `compact` | `serial` |\\n| C best-fit | `csr` | `reuse` | `serial` |\\n| D hybrid (ineligible) | `hybrid` | `append` | `pipeline` |\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --methods cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp --batches 64 --repeats 1\\n```\\n\\nFor explicit comparisons use `--cd3-kv-storage`, `--cd3-kv-csr-policy` and\\n`--cd3-kv-execution` together. Hybrid requires `--cd3-kv-csr-policy append`.\\nThe storage/publication details below describe that optional hybrid path.\\n\\nUse the same batch list, input/output lengths, KV bits and resource settings\\nwhen comparing runs. The batch list also determines maximum concurrency and\\nHBM KV reservation, so B64 alone and the B64 portion of a B64/B128 run are not\\nidentical A/B conditions. Run without `--breakdown` for performance; enable it\\nonly in separate diagnostics because its synchronization changes execution.\\n\\n## Storage and publication\\n\\nThe encoder writes codes, sign/mantissa, bases and tile offsets directly into\\nthe existing fixed body pool using physical slot IDs. Its Packed20 exception\\nwords and true exception counts use separate worker/chunk scratch rows. The\\nbody is never copied from encoder scratch into a variable-length record.\\n\\nAfter each encoded chunk, a native operation reserves entries space, copies\\nonly the actual words, and creates an immutable pending batch. K/V entries use\\nrequest-owned segments in one shared, bounded arena pool. Whole backing arenas\\nare reserved during warmup; runtime segment allocation uses a native free list\\nand append offsets. It never searches the hugepage allocator's occupied-block\\nlist. There is no Python per-record tensor-view/copy loop.\\n\\nThe main thread publishes only records whose captured slot, generation and\\nimmutable ownership still match. A K or V exception overflow keeps the true\\ncounts, omits the compressed route, and restores both sides from authoritative\\nraw secondary KV. Zero-entry records need no entries segment.\\n\\nThe old maximum-sized entries pool and append-only layer CSR arena are absent\\nin hybrid mode. The original compressed-host allowance is partitioned into\\nfixed bodies, counts, bounded entries scratch, native metadata/workspace, and\\nentries arena capacity. Segment slack and retired reader-held storage consume\\nthat same capacity. Exhaustion raises explicitly; it does not allocate another\\nhidden pool. CSR remains an explicit comparison/fallback path.\\n\\n## Planning, transfer and lifetime\\n\\nOne native record table maps each block generation to its body slot and K/V\\nentry ranges. Planning visits active IDs once, sorts physical body slots once\\nfor both sides, merges adjacent body rows, and gathers exactly the selected\\nentries ranges. Body order and entries storage order can differ; per-row entry\\noffsets connect them. Dead or inactive entries are not transferred as gaps.\\n\\nOne relative plan serves both staging rings. Native submission resolves the\\nselected ring's destination addresses. K body, entries and routing copies are\\nsubmitted together before the K completion event. K restoration can then run\\nwhile V copies proceed; V restoration waits for all V copies. Dense-buffer\\nreuse and the full-KV attention barrier remain unchanged.\\n\\nEntry reader leases retain segments through their final H2D completion.\\nReusable pinned routing snapshots are also returned only after completion.\\nFixed-body writers wait for earlier layer H2D before overwriting a reused slot.\\nConsumed events protect both staging contents and routing through decoder\\nlaunches. Final-reference free does not synchronize CUDA; explicit shutdown\\ndrains work before releasing the store.\\n\\nFull-block-only ownership is required. Legacy partial-block operation uses CSR\\nand reports `requires_full_block_only`. All paths require separate load/decode\\n# tiered-serve\\n\\nGH200의 HBM과 Grace LPDDR를 함께 사용해 vLLM V1의 weight/KV offloading과\\ncompression을 실험하는 런타임이다.\\n\\nvLLM은 request scheduling, canonical KV block ID와 model execution을\\n소유한다. `tiered-serve`는 YAML 기반 weight 배치, LPDDR/HBM 저장소,\\ncompression과 CUDA transfer/event를 소유한다. 두 저장소는 patched model\\nloader, scheduler callback, CUDA graph wrapper와 dense attention buffer를\\n통해 연결된다.\\n\\n현재 기준 경로는 GH200, vLLM V1, TP=1, KV block size 16이며 EngineCore와\\nexecutor worker가 같은 process에서 실행된다.\\n이 저장소만으로는 동작하지 않으며 sibling vLLM과 vLLM-FlashAttention에\\n[저장된 patch](patches)가 반영되어 있어야 한다. PyTorch는\\n`70d99e998b4955e0049d13a98d77ae1b14db1f45` 커밋의 수정 없는 소스와\\n그 소스에 일치하는 native 바이너리를 사용한다.\\n\\n- [CD3 KV 혼합형](docs/cd3-kv-hybrid.md): 고정 body와 entries segment, 실행 모드와 수명 관리\\n- [구조와 개발 가이드](docs/LANDING_GUIDE.md): vLLM 연동, 데이터 경로,\\n  CUDA 불변조건과 patch 검증\\n- [Inference 수행 흐름](docs/INFERENCE_FLOW.md): engine/server startup과\\n  request별 prefill/decode 실행 순서\\n- [핵심 클래스와 상태](docs/CORE_CLASSES.md): runtime owner, 주요 변수,\\n  KV ID namespace와 lifetime\\n- [기능 조합 테스트](docs/EXPERIMENT_GUIDE.md): 8B 12개, 70B 6개\\n  weight/KV offload·compression correctness matrix\\n- [Offline 실행](docs/OFFLINE_GUIDE.md): 단일 correctness, route 계측과\\n  성능 반복 실행\\n- [Serving 실행](docs/SERVING_GUIDE.md): server 기동, API 확인, 로그 수집과\\nREADME.md:19:- [CD3 KV 혼합형](docs/cd3-kv-hybrid.md): 고정 body와 entries segment, 실행 모드와 수명 관리\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0d3ce-2510-7293-8853-769c40bce311","create_time":1790260547.7601383}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
